<title>ITALY: Rinascente sees better profits in 1996.</title>
<headline>Rinascente sees better profits in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's largest quoted retail group Rinascente on Tuesday said that it expected better profits in 1996 when compared with 1995.</p>
<p>In a statement following a group board meeting, Rinascente confirmed earlier data given in January this year that its 1996 sales had risen 6.9 percent to 7.169 trillion lire due largely to the consolidation of the results from the group's recent acquisition of Migliarini.</p>
<p>In 1995, Rinascente posted a consolidated net profit of 85.8 billion lire.</p>
<p>The group Rinascente, which is controlled by the Agnelli family holding company IFIL, also runs Citta Mercato and SMA supermarkets, the Upim retail chain and Brico home improvement stores.</p>
<p>((-- Mialn newsroom +392 66129502 ))</p>
